    "title": "CTA Brings Out 1920s Vintage Railcars to Celebrate Transit Agency's 78th Anniversary - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Eunice Alpasan ,\n6 hours ago As Anna Jattkowski-Hudson rode around the Loop in a vintage CTA rail car Wednesday, it brought back childhood memories of riding the same train downtown with her mother. “It reminds me of my mom, who’s not with me anymore, because she couldn’t drive, so we would have to take the train everywhere,“ said Jattkowski-Hudson, who would ride the Brown Line downtown with her mom at least once a week. “It’s so funny because now it looks old to me. Back then, it was the coolest thing ever.” Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak 1",
